{title: Auld Lang Syne}
{artist: Robert Burns}
{key: D}
{tempo: 90}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Should [D]auld ac[G]quaintance be for[D]got
And [D]never [Bm]brought to [Em]mind [A]
Should [D]auld ac[G]quaintance be for[D]got
And [G]auld lang [A]syne [D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
For [D]auld lang [G]syne, my [D]jo
For [D]auld lang [Bm]syne [A]
We'll [D]tak a cup o' [G]kindness [D]yet
For [G]auld lang [A]syne [D]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
And [D]surely [G]ye'll be your [D]pint-stowp
And [D]surely [Bm]I'll be [Em]mine [A]
And [D]we'll tak a [G]cup o' kind[D]ness yet
For [G]auld lang [A]syne [D]
{end_of_verse}
